From 366c05f0b1b035ab55d76c9966c61451719d392c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:07:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B3a v2 code: session-level shadowing, by readings V1 to V15

src/locate_pd.rs: PowerDifferenceParams::preregistered_v2 (10 km buffer, tau = 1, sigma_meas_db 2,
session_shadowing, report_share 0.5) and method id kshana-locate/power-difference/v2. session_stations
(V2 to V4: the mean of v1's per-epoch estimate over the epochs a station reports in, the
more-than-half rule, sigma_tot^2 = sigma_sh^2 + sigma_meas^2/n), session_loglik (V5: one term per
station, P0 profiled with weights 1/sigma_tot^2; None when fewer than 3 stations report, V7),
timeline_v2 (V10), the domain statement in v2's method block (V9), and gate_row scoring a session
that is not located against the method (V7). preregistered_v1, TEMPER_V1 and v1's outputs are
unchanged; the v1 test reproduces its recorded gate rows. Unit tests: v2 parameters keep v1 as
recorded, the more-than-half rule and sigma_tot, not located with fewer than 3 reporting stations,
noiseless data from the locator's own model located in the source's cell, the timeline.

examples/locate_pd_gate.rs: dev2 (seeds 3001-3200), gate2 (seeds 4001-5000), json2 and answer2.
oracle.py: a v2 mode; it agrees with the engine on development seeds 3001-3005 (regions equal,
centroids within 5e-10 m). Its V15 run on gate-input seeds 4001-4020 comes after the gate run.

Development run (V13, implementation checks only, nothing selected; kept in dev-v2.json.gz): seeds
3001-3200 give S1 0.905, S2 0.288, S3 1.50, with 8 sessions not located and 66 redraws. No gate seed
has been drawn.
